      "message": "As mentioned yesterday, in the past, when adding a delay to workaround various issues with low/drained batteries, we repeatedly failed because the battery has actually several totally different modes when it is fully drained (e.g. just low voltage / not answering gas gauge / under-voltage protection / battery internal cut-off ...) which trigger different sequences/timings when plugged back (and are notably difficult to reproduce).\n\nHere, what would be happen for example if the battery gas gauge has triggered an internal cut-off after having detected an undervoltage on the cells ?\nWill the BGATE business and the dip on PP1800_EC happens immediately (since just when we plug AC , the battery is 0V, same as not present) or later on when the battery gas gauge has closed again its FET ? (and maybe at the wrong time)",
